Let me look at the project to ground the review — how ffmpeg is consumed via cgo, and what the binaries need.
[tool:bash] {"command":"cd /home/alex/Projects/imagerion && ls -la && head -40 go.mod && echo \"---cmd---\" && ls cmd/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"---cgo refs---\" && grep -rn \"cgo\" --include=\"*.go\" -l | head -20"}
[tool:bash] {"command":"cd /home/alex/Projects/imagerion && grep -rn \"CGO_CFLAGS\\|CGO_LDFLAGS\\|pkg-config\\|#cgo\" --include=\"*.go\" | head -30"}

Diff confirms all original values preserved (digest, SHA-256, configure flags, netgo/ldflags, stages) with exactly the approved changes. The identical `COPY warmup` lines in the diff are just newline normalization.

Now the real validation — a full image build (apt + ffmpeg compile + Go build, ~10–25 min). Using `--network=host` to match your mise task:


[tool:bash] {"command":"cd /home/alex/Projects/imagerion && docker build --network=host --progress=plain -t img-build-env . 2>&1 | tail -90","timeout":3000}

Root cause: `/home/alex` is mounted **read-only** in this environment; `DOCKER_CONFIG=/tmp/dxc` redirects buildx's config dir elsewhere. Retrying the full build:

